<title>GERMANY: ALPINE SKIING-WIBERG WINS ZWIESEL SLALOM.</title>
<headline>ALPINE SKIING-WIBERG WINS ZWIESEL SLALOM.</headline>
<dateline>ZWIESEL, Germany 1997-01-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sweden's Pernilla Wiberg won the sixth women's World Cup slalom of the Alpine skiing season on Sunday when she clocked an aggregate time of one minute 33.52 seconds for the two runs, according to provisional results.  </p>
<p>Austria's Elfi Eder was second in 1:35.21 and Italy's Deborah Compagnoni was third with 1:35.60.</p>
